{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787961620629241002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"royalistic-gorgeable-norwayrat","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"e38f15f2cd790ab871d969c6e87446efd58bf6fc625b7c88744e2f190f3236ac","event_uuid":"0753e6f4-0ad5-4586-b405-d50325fed51e","position":{"commit_sha":"b28b78cd04ded7ffb5f4d0b6e5c433e3c4cf0f68","position":"1787961609751250001-0753e6f4-0ad5-4586-b405-d50325fed51e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e970426f2b6b98092ba5d37b58274071ca850b84cafc91fb3e9ffe01884e75b1","event_uuid":"bd27a086-268c-47c4-8644-d87a97b08255","position":{"commit_sha":"58ab41aea5b4b9a046c88fa72c01b9ec56824910","position":"1787961620629241001-bd27a086-268c-47c4-8644-d87a97b08255"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787961609751250001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bd27a086-268c-47c4-8644-d87a97b08255","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"5ec7-d681-9616-43ed"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nThe MCP container image installs no `acli` (Atlassian CLI) binary, so every Jira-MUTATING bridge\noperation on the deployed box fails at the transport with `[Errno 2] No such file or directory:\n'acli'`. The Jira credentials are now correctly wired and authenticate; the binary that would use\nthem is absent.\n\n## How it was found\n\nDiscovered while verifying `colourless-hasteless-lamb`, whose fix wired `JIRA_URL`, `JIRA_USER`,\n`JIRA_PROJECT` and `JIRA_API_TOKEN` into the container. That fix moved `bridge_check_access` past\nits credential gate and, in doing so, EXPOSED this defect — it was previously masked, because the\nprobe fail-closed on `missing_credentials` before ever reaching the transport.\n\n## Observed (live, deployed container `rebar-mcp-25ea12c200ae-8092`, one run)\n\n    rebar.bridge_check_access()\n    {\n      \"steps\": [\n        {\n          \"step\": \"STEP_CREATE\",\n          \"passed\": false,\n          \"reason\": \"exception\",\n          \"detail\": \"[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'acli'\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"verdict\": \"FAIL\"\n    }\n\nIt fails at the FIRST step, `STEP_CREATE`, so `issue_key` stays `None`, the `finally` cleanup is a\nno-op and nothing is left behind in Jira. Independently confirmed: a JQL census of\n`project = REB AND summary ~ \"rebar capability probe\"` returned 0 before and 0 after.\n\n## Established by inspection\n\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp` installs `git`, `openssh-client`, `ca-certificates`, `uv`, and the\n  rebar package (`uv sync --locked --no-dev --extra agents --extra mcp --extra bedrock`). There is\n  no `acli` install step.\n- `grep -rn \"acli\\|atlassian\" infra/compose/Dockerfile.*` returns NOTHING — no image in the compose\n  stack provisions it, not just the mcp one.\n- The dependency is real and load-bearing: `applier._load_acli()` resolves the transport, and\n  `_backend.py:218` documents the CRUD transport against the remote tracker as\n  \"today: `acli.AcliClient`\".\n\n## Scope of the impact\n\nThe credentials themselves are proven good, so this is narrower than \"Jira is broken\":\n\n- Jira-MUTATING paths are DEAD on the box: `bridge_check_access`, and `reconcile` in\n  `bootstrap-strict` / `bootstrap-throttle` / `live`.\n- Direct-REST paths still work. Verified live from inside the same container: authenticated\n  `GET /rest/api/3/myself` -> 200 and `GET /rest/api/3/project/REB` -> 200, and a JQL search via\n  `POST /rest/api/3/search/jql` returned 12 real REB issues.\n\nSo the failure is specifically the `acli` subprocess transport, not connectivity, not the\ncredentials, and not the project scope.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The mcp container image provisions an `acli` binary on `PATH`, pinned to an explicit version\n      (no floating \"latest\"), with its provenance recorded the way the other pinned tools in the\n      image are.\n- [ ] A test asserts the image declares the `acli` install, so its removal cannot regress silently.\n- [ ] `bridge_check_access` run in the deployed container reaches a verdict WITHOUT a\n      `No such file or directory: 'acli'` exception at `STEP_CREATE`.\n- [ ] If `acli` is deliberately NOT to be installed, that decision is recorded instead, together\n      with what the bridge transport should be on the box, and the tools that depend on it report a\n      typed \"transport unavailable\" verdict rather than surfacing a raw `FileNotFoundError` detail.\n- [ ] No credential value is logged, printed, or committed by the fix or its verification.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["mcp","jira","bridge","infra"],"ticket_id":"54e6-ecb0-10c7-451f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP container image installs no acli binary, so every Jira-mutating bridge operation fails at the transport","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0753e6f4-0ad5-4586-b405-d50325fed51e","bd27a086-268c-47c4-8644-d87a97b08255"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787961620629241002,"uuid":"8532ee22-3ca2-4c4e-a7e3-9b98b5989b1e"}